#nexus [SplitsTree6]

BEGIN SPLITSTREE6;
DIMENSIONS nDataNodes=11 nAlgorithms=9;
PROGRAM version='SplitsTree (version dev) - License GPL v3';
WORKFLOW creationDate='1792595752328'; [Wed Oct 21 17:15:52 CEST 2026]
END; [SPLITSTREE6]

[
Methods:
Analysis was performed using RazorNet (version dev)  (Huson and Bryant 2024 ; DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.), (Hayamizu et al, 2026 ; M. Hayamizu, others, DH Huson, in preparation).
The original input consisted of 14 taxa and a 14 x 14 distance matrix.
The Razor Net method was used (default options) so as to obtain 80 nodes and 107 edges.
The Neighbor Net method (Bryant & Moulton 2004, Bryant & Huson 2023) was used (default options) so as to obtain 45 splits, circular.
The Show Splits method was used (default options) so as to obtain a Split Network visualization.
The Shave Filter method was used (default options) so as to obtain 31 nodes and 33 edges.

References:
Bryant & Huson 2023: D. Bryant and DH Huson, NeighborNet- improved algorithms and implementation. Front. Bioinform. 3, 2023.
Bryant & Moulton 2004: D. Bryant and V. Moulton. Neighbor-net: An agglomerative method for the construction of phylogenetic networks. Molecular Biology and Evolution, 21(2):255– 265, 2004.
Hayamizu et al, 2026: M. Hayamizu, others, DH Huson, in preparation
Huson and Bryant 2024: DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.
]

